share":48.5,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.0002729222727207869,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":10.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.067776010273215,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017651959752066872,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":70.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.18190001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ponce Financial Group, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Ponce Bank that provides various banking products and services. It provides various deposits, including demand, NOW/IOLA, money market, individual retirement, and savings accounts; reciprocal deposits; and certificates of deposit to individuals, business entities, and non-profit organizations. The company also offers real estate-secured loans, including one-to-four family investor-owned and owner-occupied residential; multifamily residential; nonresidential property; construction and land; commercial and industrial; and business and consumer loans. In addition, it invests in securities, which consist of U.S. government and federal agency securities and securities issued by government-sponsored or owned enterprises, as well as corporate securities, mortgage-backed securities, and Federal Home Loan Bank of New York stock. Ponce Financial Group, Inc. was founded in 1960 and is headquartered in Bronx, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Carlos P. Naudon | President, CEO & Director | Age 74 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 236 people. Revenue per employee of $463K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $231K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Ponce Financial Group, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $520M market cap on $109M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 50 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.94\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 213% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1279843319998832},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 72/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the PDLB Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_PDLB_Inflection_112226101602_1795403762.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795403762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Equity Bancshares (NYSE:EQBK) versus Ponce Financial Group (NASDAQ:PDLB) Head-To-Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/equity-bancshares-nyseeqbk-versus-ponce-financial-group-nasdaqpdlb-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794827690.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (PDLB)","source":"news.sto